Density critical points from the analytic field: NCP 3, BCP 4, RCP 2, CCP 0; Poincare-Hopf sum 1 against 1 (INCOMPLETE: The bond graph has 3 nuclei, 2 bonds and 1 component(s), cycle rank 0; found n_ring - n_cage = 2. More ring than cage points than the bond graph allows: either a spurious ring point, or 2 cage point(s) were not found - cage seeding is the likely gap. 1 nucleus/nuclei carry no core density (rho below 1 at a nucleus of Z >= 5), atom number 1: a pseudopotential replaced the core there, so the density has no cusp at those nuclei and no readable shell structure around them. A missing nuclear attractor on one of them, or a spurious ring or cage point within about a bohr of one, is a property of this wavefunction and not a gap in the seeding - QTAIM is not defined on a pseudo-density inside the core radius. )
